# Clerk — publishable key
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and paste your key. .env.local is gitignored,
# so the real value never reaches the repository.
#
#   cp app/.env.example app/.env.local
#
# Where to find it: dashboard.clerk.com -> your application -> API Keys.
# It is the *Publishable* key (pk_test_ / pk_live_), never the Secret key.
#
# Why the publishable key is safe to ship: it identifies your Clerk
# application to the browser and is public by design. It cannot sign anyone
# in on its own. The SECRET key (sk_...) is the opposite — it can mint and
# verify sessions, so it belongs only on a server and must never appear in
# frontend code or in this file.
#
# Leaving the value blank is a supported configuration. With no key:
#   - no ClerkProvider is mounted
#   - no Clerk code is downloaded by any visitor
#   - the demo sign-in path runs exactly as it does today
#
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
